### Description

The lifetime association with appended values is quite cumbersome to work with, and it does not seem necessary. Is there a reason you wouldn't want to store ```String``` in ```StrHashLocal``` instead? 

Also unrelated, there is a typo for this method:

pub fn ~~exits~~ exists(&self, s: &str) -> bool {
        let h = self.local_mapping.hasher().hash_one(s);
        let key = StrHashLocal::new(s, h);
        self.local_mapping.contains_key(&key)
    }
